 someone in english  here at link i do correct if it's a one  on one and sometimes even in a group  it's hard to avoid it  if a person keeps making keeps on making  the same mistake  so we inevitably do correct to some  extent  i try not to correct  too much  and there's different kinds of mistakes  if the person uses a word that doesn't  mean what they think it does then i'm  likely to stop them and say no that's  not how we use that word in fact it's  this other word or if they use an  expression like  very often hear people say how to say  how to say  and i say well no no in terms of filler  words in english we don't say how to say  how to say we say you know i mean well  what i mean to say is so i would  recommend that they get themselves an  english filler expression rather than  something that is obviously not native  and those kinds of things are easy  to explain and relatively easy to  remember  however when it comes to things like  grammar if someone points out to me that  i have my case wrong in russian  it has no impact on me whatsoever  i must admit also if i am struggling for  a word in russian and the  my tutor gives me the word i won't  remember it  however  i will remember if i read it or i have a  better chance to remember if i read it  and that's why i have said i like  written  um  you know lists of errors especially in  today's computer age where i can import  them and save them and  flash card them if i want and so forth  um  correcting people's pronunciation i have  found to be relatively useless  in discussions i sometimes do it but  they go right back  to pronouncing things the way they like  because that's how their brain is  configured and it takes a long time to  change one's pronunciation and that's  where i recommend a lot of repetitive  listening to a limited amount of content  and even to content which focuses on  those sounds  that people have trouble with  but correcting their pronunciation in a  discussion i found to be relatively  useless  there were other comments i think was  vera who said that stronger learners  can benefit more from correction and i  think that's true if you've got a strong  base then if you are saying  just a few things wrong then it's easier  to deal with although i must say that i  have people that i deal with  in business  who speak english well well enough to do  business whether they're japanese or  german or french or swedish or whatever  and  i mean i would never correct their  english if we're having a business  discussion never  i mean they have every right to be  offended  now with some people that i know very  well like there's a gentleman i know in  sweden  and he speaks flawless english almost  sounds like an english country gentleman  but he has his swedish expressions like  instead of saying there are  many people  in the restaurant he will say it is many  people in the restaurant because that's  how it's said in swedish and no matter  how often i remind him of that he cannot  change so i'm just saying correction  yeah maybe i think it works  for in some cases it can help you become  aware of where your gaps are i like it  in writing it's better for more advanced  learners a beginner learner i mean you  would be correcting every second word  in fact i recommend that beginner  learners don't do very much talking at  all so that they can accumulate more  words and phrases you can't make a  mistake while you're listening and  reading you only make a mistake when you  start  producing the language  so now i also had a look at moses  my friend moses he did a video response  on this whole subject  and  i think he he agrees with me and i agree  with him too that that correction can  sometimes help and so you get people  saying well correction helped me and  sometimes it does  i think where moses and i agree is that  you wouldn't do it without the  permission  of the person involved  and uh i know if i'm trying to  communicate and and when i'm  communicating what's important to me is  what i want to say  because i think i'm having a meaningful  conversation and if the other person is  is interrupting me to correct me i'm not  that fond of that but other people may  be  um  one thing i should say about moses i do  recommend that you watch his videos  and what i like about his videos and i  don't always be  praising moses and then he praises me  and it looks like we've got a mutual  uh you know support society going here  but  of the people that do videos about  language  i think he is the best teacher he may  not be the best linguist i have no idea  i haven't heard him in all his different  languages  there are people who speak more  languages or who appear to speak them  better but he's a very good teacher and  that's why i would recommend you you  follow his  videos  if you're interested in language  learning or  make contact with him and the reason i  think he's a good teacher is because he  takes his time  he is patient  he is i would even use the word kindly  and the best teachers i had were  teachers who were kindly who were  genuinely interested in me  uh i think i am too impatient to be a  good teacher i think a good teacher has  to go very slowly because  the problem is  that a teacher knows something that the  student doesn't know  and so it's very easy to go charging  ahead because you're very familiar with  something  and so  and we do have to have said this about  language learning itself you almost have  to know the language before you can  study it and that's why i'm against  grammar until you're very familiar with  it you can't study the rules the rules  don't make sense  well the same is true of language  learning and i think i jump too quickly  at times i have my experience of  language learning and so based on that i  say you learn languages this way and  that way  and moses i think is closer to his  students  more in tune with where they are gives  it to them and then repeats it in a very  kindly way and and in a very encouraging  way  uh and so he i think is probably more  likely to turn on the student make them  independent  make them good language learners  which is what what he of course proposes  to do  with his videos i've never been to one  of his classes let me see if i made any  other notes here yeah one last thing uh  you know  and and both moses and i encourage  people to just enjoy themselves and  there's no right way or wrong way you  can either  uh you know i'm gonna run out of time  but the whole thing is languages are  about having fun it's not like we're  training engineers or  neurosurgeons you make a mistake it  doesn't really matter explore the  languages however you want do many or do  few  do it as thoroughly as you want or as  superficially as you want just enjoy  yourself here we go bye for now
 

